## Implement Binary Search

📌 What is Binary Search?
      Binary Search is a searching technique where we repeatedly divide the sorted array into half.

                     ⚠️ Important: Binary Search works only when the array is sorted.

===============================================================================================================

arr = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70]
target = 50

left = 0
right = len(arr) - 1

while left <= right:

    middle = (left + right) // 2

    if arr[middle] == target:
        print("Element found at index:", middle)
        break

    elif arr[middle] < target:
        left = middle + 1

    else:
        right = middle - 1

else:
    print("Element not found")
